card.statement:
Let $\k$ has characteristic zero, $L=\k (t_1, \ldots, t_n;  z_1, \ldots z_m)$, for some integers $n$, $m$, and $\mathcal M\simeq \mathbb Z^{n}$ acting by shifts on $L$. Then

- [{(1)}] $(L*\mathcal M)^G$ is birationally equivalent to $A_n(\k)\otimes \k [z_1, \ldots, z_m]$ for any pseudo-reflection group $G$;

- [{(2)}] If $L^G\simeq L$ for a given group $G$ then $(L*\mathcal M)^G$ is birationally equivalent to $A_n(\k)\otimes \k [z_1, \ldots, z_m]$.
